# matchers.py
This module provides factory functions for building transaction matchers: call each factory with matching criteria, then apply the returned callable to a `Transaction` to get a boolean result. The matchers cover case-insensitive keyword searches across payees and notes, case-insensitive regular-expression searches limited to payees, and expense transactions whose absolute amount is below a specified cent threshold.

## b1, b2
Set up the matcher module by importing regular-expression support, the callable type, and the `Transaction` model. Define `Matcher` as the shared callable shape: it accepts a `Transaction` and returns a boolean.

## keyword
Build and return a matcher that accepts any number of `words`. Lowercase the supplied words and, for each transaction, search case-insensitively through the combined payee and note text. Return `True` if at least one word occurs as a substring; with no words, the matcher returns `False` for every transaction.

## regex
Compile the supplied regular-expression `pattern` once, using case-insensitive matching, and return a matcher that searches only `tx.payee`. The matcher returns `True` when the pattern is found and `False` otherwise; invalid regular-expression syntax fails when the factory compiles the pattern.

## amount_below
Return a matcher for expense size thresholds expressed in positive cents. It accepts only transactions where `tx.is_expense` is true and whose absolute expense amount, calculated as `-tx.amount_cents`, is strictly less than `cents`; transactions at the threshold, non-expenses, and amounts that do not satisfy the comparison return `False`.
